{{Quote box|width=30%|align=right|quote="I just wanted to do something real colorful and cutesy. This is an icy world, it's a sexy world, it's a playful world. Of course I have lots of eye candy for my girls and my boys [...] We have a lot of little surprises in store for this particular video, [...] I would like to put out 50 videos. The videos really tell the story a lot more elaborately than just the song does."|source=Minaj explaining the video's inspiration.<ref name="Superbassvideo"/>}}

On March 10, 2011, Minaj revealed during an interview with [[MTV News]] that she was shooting a video for "Super Bass" with director [[Sanaa Hamri]] and producers: Kimberly S. Stuckwisch, Michelle Larkin & Keith "KB" Brown. She explained the video's concept, stating that she wanted the video to be full of eye candy and that she wanted it to be colorful.<ref name="Superbassvideo"/><ref name="rap-up1">{{cite web |last=Lazerine |first=Devin |date=March 10, 2011 |title=Video: On Set of Nicki Minaj's 'Super Bass' |url=http://www.rap-up.com/2011/03/10/video-on-set-of-nicki-minajs-super-bass/ |access-date=May 6, 2011 |work=Rap-Up |publisher= |archive-date=September 17, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240917093401/https://www.rap-up.com/article/2011/03/10/video-on-set-of-nicki-minajs-super-bass |url-status=dead }}</ref> On April 26, 2011, Minaj premiered a sneak peek of the music video on ''[[Black Entertainment Television|BET]]'s [[106 & Park]]''.<ref name="rap-up2">{{cite web |last=Lazerine |first=Devin |date=April 26, 2011 |title=Sneak Peek: Nicki Minaj – 'Super Bass' |url=http://www.rap-up.com/2011/04/26/sneak-peek-nicki-minaj-super-bass/ |access-date=May 6, 2011 |work=Rap-Up |publisher= |archive-date=March 15, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160315183002/http://www.rap-up.com/2011/04/26/sneak-peek-nicki-minaj-super-bass/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> The preview showed Minaj in a pink wig with similarly-clad backup dancers gyrating to the song, wearing a uniform of white tank tops, denim short shorts, different colored bras, and different colored work boots and the same laces.<ref name="rap-up2"/>

Originally the video was set to premiere on the same show as where the preview was premiered on April 27, 2011, but instead was postponed. Minaj took to [[Twitter]] to explain that the music video has been pulled from the show and would not be premiering that date for unknown reasons.<ref name="rap-up2"/> The music video instead premiered on Minaj's official [[Vevo]] account on May 5, 2011.<ref name="rap-up3">{{cite web |last=Lazerine |first=Devin |title=Video: Nicki Minaj – 'Super Bass' |url=http://www.rap-up.com/2011/05/05/video-nicki-minaj-super-bass/ |access-date=2011-05-06 |work=Rap-Up |publisher= |archive-date=May 9, 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110509025150/http://www.rap-up.com/2011/05/05/video-nicki-minaj-super-bass |url-status=dead }}</ref> As of April 2024, the music video has 1.02 billion views on YouTube.

sections.text:
{{Quote box|width=30%|align=right|quote="I just wanted to do something real colorful and cutesy. This is an icy world, it's a sexy world, it's a playful world. Of course I have lots of eye candy for my girls and my boys [...] We have a lot of little surprises in store for this particular video, [...] I would like to put out 50 videos. The videos really tell the story a lot more elaborately than just the song does."|source=Minaj explaining the video's inspiration.}}

On March 10, 2011, Minaj revealed during an interview with MTV News that she was shooting a video for "Super Bass" with director Sanaa Hamri and producers: Kimberly S. Stuckwisch, Michelle Larkin & Keith "KB" Brown. She explained the video's concept, stating that she wanted the video to be full of eye candy and that she wanted it to be colorful. On April 26, 2011, Minaj premiered a sneak peek of the music video on BET's 106 & Park. The preview showed Minaj in a pink wig with similarly-clad backup dancers gyrating to the song, wearing a uniform of white tank tops, denim short shorts, different colored bras, and different colored work boots and the same laces.

Originally the video was set to premiere on the same show as where the preview was premiered on April 27, 2011, but instead was postponed. Minaj took to Twitter to explain that the music video has been pulled from the show and would not be premiering that date for unknown reasons. The music video instead premiered on Minaj's official Vevo account on May 5, 2011. As of April 2024, the music video has 1.02 billion views on YouTube.

